00:11:31.845 --> 00:11:34.097
I think this is America

00:11:34.097 --> 00:11:36.952
and everybody who wants
to run, should run.

00:11:36.952 --> 00:11:39.902
I'm very intrigued by the
story that's come out about

00:11:39.902 --> 00:11:42.966
him hiring actors to be at his pep rally.

00:11:42.966 --> 00:11:43.918
I thought that was funny

00:11:43.918 --> 00:11:45.173
mainly because I was blown away

00:11:45.173 --> 00:11:46.914
that somebody would actually
do it for 50 dollars

00:11:46.914 --> 00:11:48.794
for the whole thing all day.

00:11:48.794 --> 00:11:49.712
- [Steve] You do know what it's like

00:11:49.712 --> 00:11:50.745
being an actor in the city?

00:11:50.745 --> 00:11:52.462
- Clearly, I don't.

00:11:52.462 --> 00:11:53.925
Because I think you can go to Goodwill

00:11:53.925 --> 00:11:55.761
for two hours, buy stuff,
and sell it on Ebay

00:11:55.761 --> 00:11:56.990
and make more than 50 bucks.

00:11:56.990 --> 00:11:58.655
Take that, all you actors.

00:11:58.655 --> 00:12:00.280
There's a hack for you.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:01.564
I think that,

00:12:03.374 --> 00:12:06.117
I think he says a lot of outlandish stuff.

00:12:06.117 --> 00:12:08.856
I think that America is
more divided than ever

00:12:08.856 --> 00:12:10.063
on the left and right

00:12:10.063 --> 00:12:11.874
because people are self-selecting

00:12:11.874 --> 00:12:13.430
what they wanna listen to now

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:14.822
because you do have Fox and CNN.

00:12:14.822 --> 00:12:16.147
You have the internet where you can go to

00:12:16.147 --> 00:12:17.424
very left and right places

00:12:17.424 --> 00:12:19.556
and I think it's an intriguing
thing that's happening

00:12:19.556 --> 00:12:21.579
in general in social media right now

00:12:21.579 --> 00:12:22.972
which is I'm very concerned

00:12:22.972 --> 00:12:26.548
that people are not getting
rounded scenarios to the world

00:12:26.548 --> 00:12:28.430
because it's so easy for you to just go

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:30.427
directly into what you believe

00:12:30.427 --> 00:12:32.191
and you're having a very
intriguing thing happen

00:12:32.191 --> 00:12:34.489
in college where people are
seeing who their roommates are

00:12:34.489 --> 00:12:36.115
on Facebook before they go now,

00:12:36.115 --> 00:12:37.531
figuring out who they are,

00:12:37.531 --> 00:12:41.154
and then, kind of, asking out
and pairing up with, like,

00:12:41.154 --> 00:12:43.940
I'm a hipster and I wanna
room with a hipster.

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:46.214
I've always been very proud of myself

00:12:46.214 --> 00:12:47.539
in doing controversial things

00:12:47.539 --> 00:12:50.395
like, for example, in
the height of post-9/11,

00:12:50.395 --> 00:12:52.717
going online, scared that I was going

00:12:52.717 --> 00:12:55.363
to Al Jazeera's website
to watch the stream

00:12:55.363 --> 00:12:56.409
because I was, like, am I being,

00:12:56.409 --> 00:12:57.871
'cause I already knew I was being watched

00:12:57.871 --> 00:12:59.663
before everybody knew
they were being watched.

00:12:59.663 --> 00:13:00.801
And I go I hope they're not mad at this

00:13:00.801 --> 00:13:02.357
because I really do, you know,

00:13:02.357 --> 00:13:05.515
don't forget I'm a
child of a Soviet family

00:13:05.515 --> 00:13:07.419
whose mother wrote a book report

00:13:07.419 --> 00:13:09.648
that Fidel Castro was the
bravest man in the world

00:13:09.648 --> 00:13:11.018
and believed it in her heart and soul

00:13:11.018 --> 00:13:11.853
that this little country

00:13:11.853 --> 00:13:13.827
right next to this bad empire America

00:13:13.827 --> 00:13:15.545
and then I grew up in
America and so, like,

00:13:15.545 --> 00:13:17.310
there's always different perspectives.

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:19.493
I think Donald will absolutely resonate

00:13:19.493 --> 00:13:24.493
with a small segment of
people on the right side.

00:13:24.637 --> 00:13:28.977
I'd be flabbergasted if
he won the nomination,

00:13:28.977 --> 00:13:32.158
but I think, my intuition net net

00:13:32.158 --> 00:13:35.862
is Donald has the capability of surfacing

00:13:35.862 --> 00:13:38.323
a conversation during this process

00:13:38.323 --> 00:13:39.600
that could be healthy.

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:43.292
And I do believe that anybody
to the extremes of anything

00:13:43.292 --> 00:13:45.800
have that potential and I'm hoping

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:49.596
that weirdly that gets people,

00:13:49.596 --> 00:13:51.233
reminds people we're more aligned

00:13:51.233 --> 00:13:54.158
than we're different and
right now it's really intense

00:13:54.158 --> 00:13:56.991
in US politics in my opinion
on how separated we are

00:13:56.991 --> 00:13:59.940
and so my hope, as an optimist,
'cause that's who I am.

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:02.912
He brings a singular issue
during his short run,

00:14:02.912 --> 00:14:04.978
'cause I don't see him
winning the nomination,

00:14:04.978 --> 00:14:07.881
though he could, that
may actually bring value

00:14:07.881 --> 00:14:09.042
to the conversation.

00:14:09.042 --> 00:14:11.611
I'm intrigued by that potential

00:14:11.611 --> 00:14:13.616
probably more than anything.

00:14:13.616 --> 00:14:15.404
That was a pretty,

00:14:15.404 --> 00:14:16.285
that was a way better answer

00:14:16.285 --> 00:14:17.330
than I thought was coming.

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:18.260
(laughter)

00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:19.536
Snuck some things in, Sid you liked that?

00:14:19.536 --> 00:14:21.116
We haven't shown Sid the intern yet.

00:14:21.116 --> 00:14:24.412
Just show him.

00:14:24.412 --> 00:14:26.712
(laughter)

00:14:26.712 --> 00:14:27.849
Showed you.

00:14:27.849 --> 00:14:30.152
- [DRock] You didn't say Ricky.

00:14:30.152 --> 00:14:31.220
- In the episode?

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:32.753
Right, I always use Ricky

00:14:32.753 --> 00:14:34.169
but when I was actually answering Ricky,

00:14:34.169 --> 00:14:36.050
I barely said Ricky.

00:14:36.050 --> 00:14:36.774
Ricky.

00:14:36.774 --> 00:14:38.650
- Ted Rubin here @TedRubin on Twitter

00:14:38.650 --> 00:14:40.369
and Gary, the question I have for you

00:14:40.369 --> 00:14:42.133
is about all this talk you've had about

00:14:42.133 --> 00:14:43.178
self-awareness lately

00:14:43.178 --> 00:14:45.778
and I love the idea of
understanding what our talents are

00:14:45.778 --> 00:14:47.659
and what they're not but my fear

00:14:47.659 --> 00:14:49.679
is that we're gonna get into a mindset

00:14:49.679 --> 00:14:51.165
of things we can and can't do.

00:14:51.165 --> 00:14:52.860
Robert Browning says, "A man's reach

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:54.092
should exceed his grasp."

00:14:54.092 --> 00:14:55.902
I want people think that they can try

00:14:55.902 --> 00:14:57.784
and do a lot of different things

00:14:57.784 --> 00:14:59.571
and I'm afraid it'll bleed to our children

00:14:59.571 --> 00:15:01.428
and make them start saying
what they're good at

00:15:01.428 --> 00:15:03.076
and what they're not good at.

00:15:03.076 --> 00:15:04.517
Let me know how you feel about that

00:15:04.517 --> 00:15:05.701
and how you can incorporate that

00:15:05.701 --> 00:15:07.024
into your self-awareness talk.

00:15:07.024 --> 00:15:08.603
- Ted, big ups to you.

00:15:08.603 --> 00:15:10.623
First and foremost, you've
been, you know, again,

00:15:10.623 --> 00:15:12.480
back to the theme of the show

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:13.455
not digging fully deep,

00:15:13.455 --> 00:15:14.965
I'm not completely sure
but it's been really fun

00:15:14.965 --> 00:15:17.263
to watch from afar of
you amassing an audience

00:15:17.263 --> 00:15:20.457
and people really respect
you and kudos, do your thing.

00:15:20.457 --> 00:15:23.714
I think this is a great
question and a challenging one.

00:15:23.714 --> 00:15:25.808
First and foremost, here's
the way I answer it.

00:15:25.808 --> 00:15:26.644
This.

00:15:26.644 --> 00:15:30.142
Nothing completely one way
or the other is ever healthy.

00:15:30.142 --> 00:15:32.140
You should always be
pulling from directions,

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:33.555
finding a blend.

00:15:33.555 --> 00:15:37.433
I will say that I think people
are way more, at this point,

00:15:37.433 --> 00:15:41.311
June 2015, in belief that
they can do anything,

00:15:41.311 --> 00:15:43.377
are good at everything,
should try everything,

00:15:43.377 --> 00:15:44.887
should work on their weaknesses

00:15:44.887 --> 00:15:47.000
so I believe that I'm being aggressive

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.415
in starting a conversation
that lends itself

00:15:49.415 --> 00:15:51.991
to like drawing a line of
strengths and weaknesses

00:15:51.991 --> 00:15:53.732
that I think is very small.

00:15:53.732 --> 00:15:55.079
I do not believe this
is a big conversation.

00:15:55.079 --> 00:15:57.192
I believe modern parenting is like,

00:15:57.192 --> 00:16:00.117
hey little Steve, you
can do anything you want.

00:16:00.117 --> 00:16:01.674
Steve sucks at basketball.

00:16:01.674 --> 00:16:02.835
(laughter)

00:16:02.835 --> 00:16:04.946
He can't do everything he wants

00:16:04.946 --> 00:16:06.456
and the amount of people
that want to play basketball

00:16:06.456 --> 00:16:10.078
for a living or sing or
wanna be an engineer.

00:16:10.078 --> 00:16:11.612
You know, like a, entrepreneur,

00:16:11.612 --> 00:16:13.493
I mean you know how I feel about that.

00:16:13.493 --> 00:16:17.160
So, I think that, Ted,
I think you're right.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:19.321
I think right at this moment,

00:16:19.321 --> 00:16:22.547
my point of view on this is so small

00:16:22.547 --> 00:16:24.079
compared to the overall conversatIon

00:16:24.079 --> 00:16:25.774
that I'm going 100% all in

00:16:25.774 --> 00:16:28.701
and I don't want to hedge
against it with your point

00:16:28.701 --> 00:16:30.280
which is correct

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:33.461
because I think the whole
market's hedging against it

00:16:33.461 --> 00:16:35.198
and thus, I'm just trying to crackle it.

00:16:35.198 --> 00:16:36.520
It's the same way I talk
about social media marketing

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:37.751
versus traditional TV.

00:16:37.751 --> 00:16:40.932
I believe in TV but I don't
need to advocate for TV.

00:16:40.932 --> 00:16:43.116
99% of the market's advocating for TV.

00:16:43.116 --> 00:16:46.129
I believe that the
market, 90% of the market

00:16:46.129 --> 00:16:48.562
is advocating for you
can do whatever you want,

00:16:48.562 --> 00:16:51.111
you should try to do everything,
you should push yourself.

00:16:51.111 --> 00:16:52.635
They package it in you
should try new things

00:16:52.635 --> 00:16:53.660
and push yourself.

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:55.806
I don't think people
are talking enough about

00:16:55.806 --> 00:16:57.788
be very self-aware, know
what you're good at,

00:16:57.788 --> 00:17:00.669
force yourself, guys,

00:17:00.669 --> 00:17:02.354
I don't know if you've broken this down.

00:17:02.354 --> 00:17:04.165
Do you know what forcing yourself

00:17:04.165 --> 00:17:07.973
to be self-aware, do you know
what that process entails?

00:17:07.973 --> 00:17:11.317
Drinking a shit-load of humble kool-aid.

00:17:11.317 --> 00:17:13.615
Uh-huh, like it's insane

00:17:13.615 --> 00:17:15.635
of how much, like,

00:17:15.635 --> 00:17:17.423
it's why I talk about liking to lose.

00:17:17.423 --> 00:17:20.813
Like, it's insane of how much humility

00:17:20.813 --> 00:17:24.435
I've had to instill to now
make it optically look like

00:17:24.435 --> 00:17:28.127
I have too much ego and self-esteem.

00:17:28.127 --> 00:17:29.777
So many of you, the first
time you consumed me,

00:17:29.777 --> 00:17:31.983
some of you, like I'm really
getting in my Facebook mentions

00:17:31.983 --> 00:17:33.119
as a lot of you have noticed.

00:17:33.119 --> 00:17:34.373
Plenty of people sharing my stuff

00:17:34.373 --> 00:17:36.208
and their friends are
saying screw this guy,

00:17:36.208 --> 00:17:38.794
ego for days, full of himself.

00:17:38.794 --> 00:17:41.920
I get it but what it actually is

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:44.938
is the post game of me being really humble

00:17:44.938 --> 00:17:46.633
every minute of my life to recognize

00:17:46.633 --> 00:17:48.444
what I should stay away from.

00:17:48.444 --> 00:17:50.349
And I think people have
not gotten into that gear

00:17:50.349 --> 00:17:53.855
so Ted I would say that I
get it and I agree with you.

00:17:53.855 --> 00:17:56.454
And everything should
have a push and a pull.

00:17:56.454 --> 00:17:59.612
I just think the market is way, way

00:17:59.612 --> 00:18:03.049
in the direction of (pats Steve's back)

00:18:03.049 --> 00:18:05.557
and I think that we need a
hell of a more a lot of like

00:18:05.557 --> 00:18:07.670
you kinda suck at that, you
may want to focus on that.

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:12.437
Now, if you love that, then do it.

00:18:12.437 --> 00:18:14.636
But you need to know what
that comes along with

00:18:14.636 --> 00:18:18.745
which is if you love singing
more than breathing, cool

00:18:18.745 --> 00:18:20.207
but you're gonna wait tables

00:18:20.207 --> 00:18:22.204
and you're gonna make eight bucks

00:18:22.204 --> 00:18:23.342
and that's great!

00:18:23.342 --> 00:18:24.387
Because guess what?

00:18:24.387 --> 00:18:26.036
I pay the price for doing what I love

00:18:26.036 --> 00:18:27.452
in a lot of different ways.

00:18:27.452 --> 00:18:29.693
And so that's just life.

00:18:29.693 --> 00:18:31.282
That's just life.

00:18:33.076 --> 00:18:34.348
Cool.

